the target language is: prolog.

% Spike: the trap of the design notes l4.md, section 7 -- in the Prolog
% target the min of an empty set is 0, so both queries answer 0, not nothing.

the templates are:
    *a party* pays at *a time*; undefined.
    the first payment in the window is at *a time*.
    the first payment in the window from *a start* to *an end* is at *a time*.

the knowledge base agg includes:

the first payment in the window is at a time if
    the time is the min of each moment such that
        bob pays at the moment
        and the moment >= 10
        and the moment =< 40.

the first payment in the window from a start to an end is at a time if
    the time is the min of each moment such that
        bob pays at the moment
        and the moment >= the start
        and the moment =< the end.

query q is:
    the first payment in the window is at which time.

query r is:
    the first payment in the window from 10 to 40 is at which time.

scenario s is:
    bob pays at 5.
    bob pays at 50.
    q expects answers ["the first payment in the window is at nothing"].
    r expects answers ["the first payment in the window from 10 to 40 is at nothing"].
